<subpara id="RM000000URQ00GX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___00005X100000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<step1>
<ptxt>Inspect Power Steering Computer Assembly</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), inspect the voltage, continuity or resistance between each pair of terminals or between each terminal and body ground.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>With the connector connected to the computer, inspect from the back side of the connector.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When the P/S warning light is illuminated (malfunction), the terminal voltage of the power steering control computer assembly may be 0V due to the fail-safe function.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>As connector A uses a connector with a lock lever, the terminals cannot be inspected with the connector connected to the power steering computer assembly.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), check that pulses are generated between each pair of terminals or between each terminal and body ground.</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3, and check the communication status with the power steering computer assembly.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
